            {
              "id": "modelling_plan",
              "name": "Modelling plan (for Blender / engine agents)",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "POTTED PLANT — MODELLING PLAN (surface draft; to be refined)\nMetres unless stated; values in braces are this object's parameters. Z up, floor at Z 0. Hosted on a point: origin at the placement point on the floor.\n\nWHAT IT IS\nlarge-leaved indoor plant in an ivory pot, healthy\n\nGEOMETRY\nModel the object described above as clean, closed meshes with real thickness and small bevels on exposed edges (about 2 mm) so highlights catch. Drive every dimension from these parameters:\n- Pot diameter: {potDia}\n- Pot height: {potHeight}\n- Soil below the rim: {soilDrop}\n- Trunk height: {trunkHeight}\n- Trunk radius: {trunkRadius}\n- Leaves: {leaves}\n- Tiers: {tiers}\n- Leaf length: {leafLength}\n- Leaf width: {leafWidth}\n- Leaf thickness: {leafThk}\n- Canopy rise: {canopyRise}\n- Droop: {droop}\n- Seed: {seed}\n- Rotation (deg): {rotation}\n- Anchor Direction: {anchorDir} (one of: Top-Left / Top-Center / Top-Right / Left-Center / Center / Right-Center / Bottom-Left / Bottom-Center / Bottom-Right)\n- Margin from host: {margin}\n- Flip side: {flipSide}\nKeep the proportions of a well-made real product; add the secondary detail a close-up render needs (joints, reveals, fixings) but no hidden interior geometry.\n\nMATERIALS\n- Base colour: {baseColor}\n- Roughness: {roughness}\nPrincipled BSDF per visible part, using the colour and roughness above for the main surface; secondary parts in a neutral complementary finish. Use Object / box-projected texture coordinates (no UVs needed). Add a subtle noise bump (strength ~0.03) so surfaces are not perfectly flat.\n\nLIGHTS\nNone. This object does not emit light.\n\nCHECKS (measure after building)\n- Pot height = {potHeight}\n- Soil below the rim = {soilDrop}\n- Trunk height = {trunkHeight}\n- Trunk radius = {trunkRadius}\n- Leaf length = {leafLength}\n- Leaf width = {leafWidth}\n- All meshes closed, no duplicate faces, origin as stated above.",
